o rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T23:56:53-07:00","id":1313453,"title":"","content":"...oh! Book of Oblivion goes live to backers this week!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T14:05:57-07:00","id":1313556,"title":"","content":"Book's live for backers.<br /> <br /> And if you find anything errata-worthy, <a href=\"https://forms.gle/v1tqsp5SRPphepyb6\" target=\"_blank\">you go here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T16:26:19-07:00","id":1313580,"title":"","content":"<i>anticipatory chittering intensifies</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T21:31:25-07:00","id":1313617,"title":"","content":"*flips through ToC*<br /> <br /> ...aw. Only one new Dark Kingdom-exclusive Arcanos? Well that's a bit of a bummer...although given the page count of this thing, I suppose not much can be done if the devs were trying to squeeze in as much as they could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T07:02:34-07:00","id":1313655,"title":"","content":"Darn, Kickstarter failed to deliver me the links for Book of Oblivion. I notified Rick by comment and PM on KS. Hope he can send them to me ASAP. I am really eager to read this one.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I got the links. Thank you to Rick for the prompt and efficient solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-22-2019, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T05:13:28-07:00","id":1313817,"title":"","content":"Aw man, the Merits &amp; Flaws weren't added to the book. I was hoping it would be added, like they were in M20's Book of Secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5402-malcolmlittle","name":"MalcolmLittle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T11:55:06-07:00","id":1313879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalcolmLittle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1313817#post1313817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw man, the Merits &amp; Flaws weren't added to the book. I was hoping it would be added, like they were in M20's Book of Secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah that I was more prepared for not having. <br /> <br /> The way how the book was initially previewed as, including the breakdown of what was in it, nothing seemed to suggest it was going to be a companion book on the level of BoS. That I figured was going to be a later book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T13:15:19-07:00","id":1314778,"title":"","content":"Clearly we need a Secrets of the Grave book at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T03:04:16-07:00","id":1316216,"title":"","content":"Is the errata deadline this Tuesday? This book seems under-developed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T11:34:44-07:00","id":1316460,"title":"","content":"nice but what about the rest of us that didnt get a chance to be backers???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24734-deadman","name":"DeadMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T11:43:26-07:00","id":1316461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316216#post1316216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the errata deadline this Tuesday?</div> </div> </div> </div>No clue. Only way to know for sure is when the errata page closes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This book seems under-developed. </div> </div> </div>...in what way?<br /> <br /> (bear in mind that from the beginning, I don't think it was ever meant to be on the same scope of, say, M20's Book of Secrets or C20's Player's Guide)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316460#post1316460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nice but what about the rest of us that didnt get a chance to be backers???</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When it's done&quot;.<br /> <br /> Meaning: errata needs to finish collection, integrated into the book, sent back to layout if necessary to accommodate for shifts in the text, get the PoD proofs to make sure everything's ok, and THEN opening it up for DrivethruRPG.<br /> <br /> All of which takes a month or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T20:41:26-07:00","id":1316547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316461#post1316461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...in what way?<br /> <br /> (bear in mind that from the beginning, I don't think it was ever meant to be on the same scope of, say, M20's Book of Secrets or C20's Player's Guide)</div> </div> </div> </div>Loads of inconsistencies with Wraith's theme and mood, even history that should have been caught by anyone with a basic knowledge of W:tO. The biggest examples are a couple of references that refer to Charon still ruling Stygia. Mathew Dawkins comment above seems to indicate that writers were chosen for diversity over experience with Wraith. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T20:43:51-07:00","id":1316549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316547#post1316547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loads of inconsistencies with Wraith's theme and mood, even history that should have been caught by anyone with a basic knowledge of W:tO. The biggest examples are a couple of references that refer to Charon still ruling Stygia. Mathew Dawkins comment above seems to indicate that writers were chosen for diversity over experience with Wraith. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Did you report said errors on the errata sheet?<br /> <br /> (And if it\u2019s a choice between the two, I definitely want writers who actually have an insider perspective on the culture they\u2019re writing about and won\u2019t fall back on exoticizing stereotypes over ones who have a game line pedigree. That said, inconsistencies like that are the job of the book developer to fix)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-04-2019, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-04T23:17:30-07:00","id":1316563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316549#post1316549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you report said errors on the errata sheet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am doing so; there's a lot. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316549#post1316549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And if it\u2019s a choice between the two, I definitely want writers who actually have an insider perspective on the culture they\u2019re writing about and won\u2019t fall back on exoticizing stereotypes over ones who have a game line pedigree. That said, inconsistencies like that are the job of the book developer to fix)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said it was under-developed. There doesn't seem to be any special insight to the cultures. The Dark Kingdom of Ivory is worse than ever and borderline offensive on the level of Chechnya in the V5 Camarilla book. The Bush of Ghosts has been turned into a plantation modeled after the slave ones, and another major area is called &quot;The Hood&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T01:02:30-07:00","id":1316571,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm about to head to bed so I can't talk about all of this, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316563#post1316563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Bush of Ghosts has been turned into a plantation modeled after the slave ones</b>, and another major area is called &quot;The Hood&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm...no it hasn't?<br /> <br /> Specifically: the Bush itself hasn't. It's only the &quot;Ivory Mirrorlands&quot; that has. And the Plantation isn't something that was forcefully imposed on the wraiths there. It's an elaborate lie that the leader, Ghede, spearheaded in an effort to save the Ivory Mirrorlands from being taken over by Ya'Qub, and to buy time so their corner of the Ivory Kingdom can prepare and ready themselves to directly fight Ya'Qub and his army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T06:42:47-07:00","id":1316620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316571#post1316571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm about to head to bed so I can't talk about all of this, but...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Uhm...no it hasn't?<br /> <br /> Specifically: the Bush itself hasn't. It's only the &quot;Ivory Mirrorlands&quot; that has. And the Plantation isn't something that was forcefully imposed on the wraiths there. It's an elaborate lie that the leader, Ghede, spearheaded in an effort to save the Ivory Mirrorlands from being taken over by Ya'Qub, and to buy time so their corner of the Ivory Kingdom can prepare and ready themselves to directly fight Ya'Qub and his army.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OK, I got the two mixed up, but the point still stands. It's not African culture, but a copy of Caribbean culture, even using the same name. It even calls it a &quot;gumbo&quot; mixed with New World cultures. (They aren't preparing to fight Ya'Qub, but hoping the One Who Sleeps will come to save them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T13:57:16-07:00","id":1316697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316620#post1316620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I got the two mixed up, but the point still stands. It's not African culture, but a copy of Caribbean culture, even using the same name. It even calls it a &quot;gumbo&quot; mixed with New World cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'm by no means an expert on the Vodou religion, culture, and it's variations, but going off from a quick scan on Wikipedia...<br /> <br /> ...what we now know as Haitian Vodou has origins in West Africa. And that we even had a sidebar saying that yes, there are two different Mirrorlands: the one that's part of the Ivory Kingdom and the other one that's part of Haiti. So it doesn't seem out of place to have that here.<br /> <br /> And the &quot;gumbo&quot; bit is supposed to be in reference to Ghede deliberately looking at other cultures that fell to colonialism in an attempt to find. Which to me, is less the writer forgetting that gumbo is from a completely different culture, but is supposed to be the ruler of a nation learning what's happening with other peoples to protect his own nation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (They aren't preparing to fight Ya'Qub, but hoping the One Who Sleeps will come to save them.) </div> </div> </div>Huh? Yeah they are. Or rather: they're doing both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T22:37:29-07:00","id":1316940,"title":"","content":"I will say the new version of the DKoI seems super concentrated on coastal regions of Central Western Africa to the detriment of detailing other areas of the continent.<br /> <br /> Using the names Plantation and Hood are weirding me out as they're not terms used in any of the african diaspora here and I'm not sure where they may have been sourced from other than the US ( which would be really weird, why not use one of the hundreds of Shona, Swahili, Igbo etc. words available...hell even French would make more sense....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-07-2019, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T06:21:36-07:00","id":1316975,"title":"","content":"There is definitely a focus on West African culture for the Dark Kingdom of Ivory, and that's a for a couple of reasons:<br /> <br /> 1.) Africa is a large continent with a multitude of myths and legends, and we preferred to explore a single region over providing light detail to dozens. <br /> 2.) Our writer (Jiba Molei Anderson) is most familiar with West African culture and history. <br /> <br /> As always, feel free to suggest amendments to text via the errata form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T22:43:32-07:00","id":1317114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1316940#post1316940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say the new version of the DKoI seems super concentrated on coastal regions of Central Western Africa to the detriment of detailing other areas of the continent.<br /> <br /> Using the names Plantation and Hood are weirding me out as they're not terms used in any of the african diaspora here and I'm not sure where they may have been sourced from other than the US ( which would be really weird, why not use one of the hundreds of Shona, Swahili, Igbo etc. words available...hell even French would make more sense....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah the Plantation and Hood thing seemed a weird choice to me. This isn't America why choose those names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T16:33:31-07:00","id":1317699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1317114#post1317114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the Plantation and Hood thing seemed a weird choice to me. This isn't America why choose those names?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plantation agriculture was a big thing in West Africa, by both local rulers and colonial interests, from the 16th to 20th century. Sugar, groundnuts, and palm oil were some of the major commercial crops, from what I understand. Hip hop is also incredibly popular in Africa (especially in Nigeria and Senegal), including a large number of local artists who fuse various American styles with more traditional African musical styles. So it's not inconceivable that the term &quot;hood&quot; might be used, especially it's part of some sort of Potemkin village set up to fool outsiders. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T16:38:03-07:00","id":1317701,"title":"","content":"Using one or the other might not be too jarring, but using both together seems to magnify the peculiarity of their usage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T01:19:10-07:00","id":1317757,"title":"","content":"The errata form has been closed. (I missed the chance to tell them the word &quot;gaunt&quot; still hasn't been defined, as are True Obsidian, True Silver, True Gold, and True Turquoise.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","user":"muon","date":". 06-11-2019, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T15:06:51-07:00","id":1317885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1317757#post1317757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The errata form has been closed. (I missed the chance to tell them the word &quot;gaunt&quot; still hasn't been defined, as are True Obsidian, True Silver, True Gold, and True Turquoise.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No biggie. If its anything like the previous errata collection threads we've had the vast majority of reported issues won't be changed anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T15:37:39-07:00","id":1317891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1317885#post1317885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No biggie. If its anything like the previous errata collection threads we've had the vast majority of reported issues won't be changed anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we are using completely different methods of collecting errata...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T19:16:26-07:00","id":1317939,"title":"","content":"Gaunts are ancient and powerful Wraiths that retain at least one Fetter. Think of them as elders or ancients in Vampire.<br /> <br /> True Obsidian, Jade, Gold, Turquoise, etc. are the localized equivalent of Stygian steel. An example would be the True Jade swords and other weapons of the Dark Kingdom of Jade. They are just as potent as Stygian Steel, just born of a substance more common to the region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T22:24:00-07:00","id":1317972,"title":"","content":"Which area uses True Silver?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T22:47:53-07:00","id":1317981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1317972#post1317972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which area uses True Silver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lands of Gold/South American Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T03:15:04-07:00","id":1318199,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you. I figured gold was theirs so I guess they get two? I presume there is a note somewhere about its impact on Werewolf crossovers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T11:38:38-07:00","id":1318272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1318199#post1318199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thank you. I figured gold was theirs so I guess they get two?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they got both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I presume there is a note somewhere about its impact on Werewolf crossovers? </div> </div> </div>There is not, no.<br /> <br /> Although the way how it's described, my impression has always been that, despite the name, they aren't actually the materials from the Skinlands side. So if you managed to bring a True Silver weapon across the Shroud and into the Skinlands, I don't think it's supposed to work like regular silver on a werewolf.<br /> <br /> In general there isn't a whole lot of crossover bits, nor are they REALLY a major focus. There's some token stuff, like hinting at Mirrorlands wraiths' interactions with the Samedi bloodline, the tense relationship between Flint wraiths and Uktena werewolves, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> The only real substantial bit of crossover (ergo involving mechanics and setting) is the Arcane Storm. Basically, it's a Tempest non-Maelstrom storm that's caused whenever a mage dies and becomes a wraith, the act of their Avatar leaving their body creates a storm.<br /> <br /> ...and naturally changelings get nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T08:10:55-07:00","id":1320755,"title":"","content":"Just to be sure we weren't barking up the wrong tree with the use of &quot;the Hood&quot; to describe the modern name for &quot;the Shade&quot; in the Dark Kingdom of Ivory, I've been doing some additional research and have spoken to the writer of that chapter. We've discussed, and while &quot;the Hood&quot; is common parlance in South Africa and a few other West African nations, we've added &quot;Komboni&quot; as an alternative name, which is the old and present name for the slums of Zambia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T23:54:24-07:00","id":1323136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1282216-book-of-oblivion?p=1320755#post1320755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be sure we weren't barking up the wrong tree with the use of &quot;the Hood&quot; to describe the modern name for &quot;the Shade&quot; in the Dark Kingdom of Ivory, I've been doing some additional research and have spoken to the writer of that chapter. We've discussed, and while &quot;the Hood&quot; is common parlance in South Africa and a few other West African nations, we've added &quot;Komboni&quot; as an alternative name, which is the old and present name for the slums of Zambia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to give general feedback: I think the issue here was context.<br /> <br /> That no proper context was given for why the term was there in the Backer PDF to bring any readers not familiar with West African culture up to speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T19:42:34-07:00","id":1330674,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, Book of Oblivion's going to finally be available for everyone this Wednesday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":